Sensor Module

The Sensor Module is responsible for collecting environmental data required for weather monitoring.
It acts as the input unit of the Weather Detection System by detecting changes in environmental conditions\
and sending the collected data to the microcontroller for processing.

The system uses different sensors to measure important weather parameters:
1. Temperature Sensor
The temperature sensor measures the surrounding air temperature and provides real-time readings.
The collected data helps users monitor environmental temperature conditions and supports weather analysis.
2. Humidity Sensor
The humidity sensor measures the amount of moisture present in the air. 
It provides humidity values in percentage form and is useful for monitoring atmospheric conditions,
especially in agriculture and environmental studies.
3. Rainfall Sensor
The rainfall sensor detects the presence and amount of rainfall.
It helps determine weather changes and provides information that can support agricultural planning and rainfall monitoring.
The sensor module continuously collects environmental data and transmits it to the microcontroller. 
The microcontroller processes the received values and displays them on the LCD while also storing the information for future reference.
The accuracy and performance of the Weather Detection System depend greatly on the sensor module because it serves as the primary source of environmental data.
Proper calibration and testing of sensors are important to ensure reliable readings.
